",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#orange\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Orange & Ginger Animal Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[5,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#gray\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Gray & Silver Animal Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[6,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#multi\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Multi-Colored & Patterned Names\"}]]}],\"$L23\",\"$L24\"]}]]}],\"$L25\",\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\",\"$L2d\",\"$L2e\",\"$L2f\",\"$L30\",\"$L31\",\"$L32\",\"$L33\",\"$L34\",\"$L35\",\"$L36\",\"$L37\",\"$L38\",\"$L39\",\"$L3a\"]}],\"$L3b\",\"$L3c\",\"$L3d\",\"$L3e\",\"$L3f\",\"$L40\"]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"li\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[7,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#rare\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Rare Color Names (Blue, Green, Purple)\"}]]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"li\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[8,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#faq\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}]]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"One of the easiest and most natural ways to name a pet is by their color. Whether you have a snow-white \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"104\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cat/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Cat\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", a jet-black \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"123\",{\"href\":\"/animal/dog/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Dog\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", or a ginger \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"142\",{\"href\":\"/animal/hamster/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Hamster\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", there is a perfect color-inspired name waiting. This guide covers every shade of the rainbow with creative, meaningful, and memorable names for animals of all colors.\"]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"White & Cream Animal Names 🤍\"]}]\n27:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"White pets have a special, ethereal beauty. Their pristine coats invite names that evoke purity, winter, and celestial brightness. Popular white pet names include <strong>Snowball</strong>, <strong>Casper</strong>, <strong>Pearl</strong>, <strong>Ghost</strong>, <strong>Blizzard</strong>, and <strong>Angel</strong>. For a cream or off-white pet, consider <strong>Vanilla</strong>, <strong>Ivory</strong>, <strong>Chantilly</strong>, <strong>Buttermilk</strong>, or <strong>Marzipan</strong>.\"}}]\n28:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Celestial white names evoke heavenly brightness: <strong>Luna</strong>, <strong>Stella</strong>, <strong>Nova</strong>, <strong>Celeste</strong>, <strong>Orion</strong>. Winter-themed names celebrate frosty beauty: <strong>Frost</strong>, <strong>Crystal</strong>, <strong>Glacier</strong>, <strong>Yuki</strong> (snow), <strong>Neve</strong> (snow). For pets with pure white coats, gemstone names like <strong>Diamond</strong>, <strong>Opal</strong>, and <strong>Moonstone</strong> shine especially bright.\"}}]\n29:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Black & Dark Animal Names 🖤\"]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Black animals possess an undeniable elegance and mystery. Their dark coats are striking canvases for names that evoke night, shadow, and sophistication. Classic black pet names: <strong>Shadow</strong>, <strong>Midnight</strong>, <strong>Onyx</strong>, <strong>Raven</strong>, <strong>Panther</strong>, <strong>Ebony</strong>, <strong>Jet</strong>, <strong>Coal</strong>.\"}}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"For refined black pets, consider sophisticated names: <strong>Noir</strong>, <strong>Obsidian</strong>, <strong>Indigo</strong>, <strong>Velvet</strong>, <strong>Licorice</strong>. Mythological dark names carry power: <strong>Hades</strong>, <strong>Nyx</strong>, <strong>Loki</strong>, <strong>Salem</strong>, <strong>Wednesday</strong>. Food-inspired black names add whimsy: <strong>Espresso</strong>, <strong>Truffle</strong>, <strong>Caviar</strong>, <strong>Olive</strong>, <strong>Pepper</strong>.\"}}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Brown & Tan Animal Names 🤎\"]}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Brown pets are warm, earthy, and comforting. Their rich coats invite names drawn from nature, food, and autumn. Popular brown names: <strong>Cocoa</strong>, <strong>Mocha</strong>, <strong>Hazel</strong>, <strong>Copper</strong>, <strong>Bruno</strong>, <strong>Maple</strong>, <strong>Autumn</strong>, <strong>Acorn</strong>.\"}}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Coffee and chocolate names are endlessly appealing: <strong>Latte</strong>, <strong>Java</strong>, <strong>Toffee</strong>, <strong>Caramel</strong>, <strong>Brownie</strong>, <strong>Fudge</strong>. Nature names connect to forests and earth: <strong>Timber</strong>, <strong>Cedar</strong>, <strong>Oakley</strong>, <strong>Clay</strong>, <strong>Dusty</strong>, <strong>Rusty</strong>. For tan or golden-brown pets, try <strong>Sandy</strong>, <strong>Amber</strong>, <strong>Topaz</strong>, <strong>Honey</strong>, <strong>Ginger</strong>.\"}}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Orange & Ginger Animal Names 🧡\"]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Orange and ginger pets are vibrant showstoppers. Their fiery, warm coats demand names as bold as their appearance. The classic orange cat name is <strong>Garfield</strong>, but there are so many more creative options.\"}}]\n31:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Food names shine for orange pets: <strong>Pumpkin</strong>, <strong>Mango</strong>, <strong>Peaches</strong>, <strong>Tangerine</strong>, <strong>Paprika</strong>, <strong>Cheddar</strong>, <strong>Cheeto</strong>, <strong>Marmalade</strong>. Fire-themed names blaze with personality: <strong>Blaze</strong>, <strong>Ember</strong>, <strong>Flame</strong>, <strong>Phoenix</strong>, <strong>Ignis</strong>. Autumn-inspired names capture the orange season: <strong>Rusty</strong>, <strong>Maple</strong>, <strong>Autumn</strong>, <strong>Marigold</strong>.\"}}]\n32:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Gray & Silver Animal Names 🩶\"]}]\n33:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Gray pets have a subtle, sophisticated beauty. From pale silver to deep charcoal, gray coats offer wonderful naming possibilities. Popular gray names: <strong>Smokey</strong>, <strong>Storm</strong>, <strong>Ash</strong>, <strong>Slate</strong>, <strong>Silver</strong>, <strong>Misty</strong>, <strong>Dusty</strong>, <strong>Pebbles</strong>.\"}}]\n34:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Metallic names gleam with cool elegance: <strong>Sterling</strong>, <strong>Platinum</strong>, <strong>Steel</strong>, <strong>Chrome</strong>, <strong>Titanium</strong>. Weather-inspired gray names add atmosphere: <strong>Foggy</strong>, <strong>Cloud</strong>, <strong>Nimbus</strong>, <strong>Thunder</strong>, <strong>Gandalf</strong> (the Grey!). For blue-gray pets, try <strong>Bluebell</strong>, <strong>Sapphire</strong>, <strong>Periwinkle</strong>.\"}}]\n35:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"17\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Multi-Colored & Patterned Names 🎯\"]}]\n36:[\"$\",\"p\",\"18\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Pets with multiple colors or striking patterns deserve names that celebrate their unique markings. Calico \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"106\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cat/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Cat\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\"s, brindle \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"122\",{\"href\":\"/animal/dog/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Dog\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\"s, spotted \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"138\",{\"href\":\"/animal/rabbit/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Rabbit\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\"s — each pattern tells its own naming story.\"]}]\n37:[\"$\",\"p\",\"19\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Patchwork names: <strong>Patches</strong>, <strong>Domino</strong>, <strong>Checkers</strong>, <strong>Pixel</strong>, <strong>Mosaic</strong>, <strong>Marble</strong>, <strong>Oreo</strong>, <strong>S'mores</strong>. Spotted names: <strong>Freckles</strong>, <strong>Speckles</strong>, <strong>Dot</strong>, <strong>Dapple</strong>, <strong>Pongo</strong> (101 Dalmatians). For pets with distinct masks or caps: <strong>Bandit</strong>, <strong>Zorro</strong>, <strong>Phantom</strong>, <strong>Rorschach</strong>.\"}}]\n38:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"20\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Rare Color Names: Blue, Green, Purple 💙💚💜\"]}]\n39:[\"$\",\"p\",\"21\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"While naturally blue, green, or purple mammals don't exist, exotic birds, fish, and reptiles come in these spectacular shades. These rare color names make unforgettable pet names.\"]}]\n3a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"22\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Blue names: <strong>Azure</strong>, <strong>Cobalt</strong>, <strong>Cerulean</strong>, <strong>Sapphire</strong>, <strong>Neptune</strong>, <strong>Lagoon</strong>, <strong>Bluebell</strong>. Green names: <strong>Emerald</strong>, <strong>Forest</strong>, <strong>Jade</strong>, <strong>Basil</strong>, <strong>Kiwi</strong>, <strong>Matcha</strong>. Purple names: <strong>Amethyst</strong>, <strong>Violet</strong>, <strong>Lilac</strong>, <strong>Lavender</strong>, <strong>Plum</strong>, <strong>Mauve</strong>.\"}}]\n3b:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should I name my pet based on their color?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Color-based names are one of the most natural and popular approaches to pet naming. They're immediately descriptive, easy for others to understand, and often lead to charming and unique name choices.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What if my pet's color changes as they grow?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Some animals do change color with age — kittens may darken, puppies may lighten. If your pet is young, choose a name inspired by their personality rather than their current color, or pick a name that works for multiple shades.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are food-themed color names too common?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"While food names like Cocoa and Ginger are popular, they are popular for good reason — they are warm, appealing, and easy for both humans and pets to recognize. Don't avoid a great name just because others use it.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are the most unique color-based names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Less common but beautiful color names include Cerulean, Amaranth, Vermillion, Saffron, Cinnabar, Perse, and Xanthe. These rare color words make distinctive, conversation-starting pet names.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n3c:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"cat\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cat/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐱\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Cat\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"dog\",{\"href\":\"/animal/dog/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐕\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Dog\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"rabbit\",{\"href\":\"/animal/rabbit/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐰\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Rabbit\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"hamster\",{\"href\":\"/animal/hamster/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"c